WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.044 --> 00:00:06.506
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:15.473 --> 00:00:20.937
Ankylosaurs were one of the most remarkable of dinosaurs.

00:00:20.937 --> 00:00:24.566
Perhaps, the most heavily armored of any animal

00:00:24.566 --> 00:00:26.568
that world has ever seen.

00:00:26.568 --> 00:00:29.863
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:33.783
They're so odd.

00:00:33.783 --> 00:00:36.244
I think they're one of the most bizarre animals.

00:00:36.244 --> 00:00:38.288
When you look at the proportions of their bodies,

00:00:38.288 --> 00:00:39.956
there are questions around how they even

00:00:39.956 --> 00:00:42.125
walked, how they moved.

00:00:42.125 --> 00:00:44.586
They had spikes extending from their shoulder

00:00:44.586 --> 00:00:48.631
regions, a bony covering of armor all over their heads.

00:00:48.631 --> 00:00:52.469
Some of them even had bony eyelids.

00:00:52.469 --> 00:00:55.054
One feature more than all the others

00:00:55.054 --> 00:00:59.809
separates them from any animal alive today--

00:00:59.809 --> 00:01:01.936
their extraordinary tail.

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:08.610
So what was it for?

00:01:08.610 --> 00:01:10.945
Some ankylosaurs have very peculiar tails,

00:01:10.945 --> 00:01:13.114
where they take the armor on other parts of the body

00:01:13.114 --> 00:01:17.911
and elaborate it into what we call a tail club.

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:20.121
These are two huge lumps of armor

00:01:20.121 --> 00:01:24.125
that are fused to the very last few vertebrae within the tail

00:01:24.125 --> 00:01:28.171
and form this structure a little bit like a hammer.

00:01:28.171 --> 00:01:30.381
When they were first discovered, they

00:01:30.381 --> 00:01:34.511
were interpreted as a weapon of some kind.

00:01:34.511 --> 00:01:36.930
This one belonged to a kind of ankylosaur,

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:39.724
known as anodontosaur.

00:01:39.724 --> 00:01:42.352
But what makes us think that this was ever

00:01:42.352 --> 00:01:43.895
wielded like a club?

00:01:43.895 --> 00:01:47.148
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:47.649 --> 00:01:51.152
Comparing ankylosaurs with animals alive today

00:01:51.152 --> 00:01:55.031
suggests that it was.

00:01:55.031 --> 00:01:57.575
On numerous occasions within the history of life,

00:01:57.575 --> 00:02:00.161
animals have evolved specialized structures

00:02:00.161 --> 00:02:03.289
that only function in combat.

00:02:03.289 --> 00:02:06.167
These are often quite large and unusual structures,

00:02:06.167 --> 00:02:11.089
like the horns of rhinos, the antlers of deer,

00:02:11.089 --> 00:02:15.051
the horns of antelope.

00:02:15.051 --> 00:02:18.137
Powerful muscles and reinforced bone

00:02:18.137 --> 00:02:20.598
allow them to use these structures as weapons.

00:02:23.685 --> 00:02:29.190
Fossils show ankylosaur tails had similar adaptations.

00:02:29.190 --> 00:02:32.568
There's evidence on the pelvis for muscles that extended down

00:02:32.568 --> 00:02:34.404
the tail and that would have attached

00:02:34.404 --> 00:02:38.324
to the handle of this tail club.

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:39.450
It's very stiff.

00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:41.244
It's stiffened by lots of bony rods

00:02:41.244 --> 00:02:43.121
that run along the length of the tail that

00:02:43.121 --> 00:02:44.747
would have had a lot of force behind it

00:02:44.747 --> 00:02:47.083
when it was swung from side to side.

00:02:47.083 --> 00:02:48.876
Some paleontologists have calculated

00:02:48.876 --> 00:02:50.670
that it could be swung with enough force

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:54.132
to devastate a car.

00:02:54.132 --> 00:02:57.593
It would have made a formidable weapon to defend itself

00:02:57.593 --> 00:02:58.386
against enemies.

00:03:03.307 --> 00:03:06.936
But now, scientists are asking a new question.

00:03:06.936 --> 00:03:10.148
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:03:11.524 --> 00:03:15.319
In theory, ankylosaur tails would

00:03:15.319 --> 00:03:17.989
have been able to break the legs of predators.

00:03:17.989 --> 00:03:23.244
But it's possible that they were also using their tail clubs

00:03:23.244 --> 00:03:27.290
for fighting a rival for a mate, or to be

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:28.791
the leader of the pack.

00:03:28.791 --> 00:03:31.919
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:03:33.337 --> 00:03:37.592
In fact, the most recent study from 2022

00:03:37.592 --> 00:03:40.386
reveals injuries among ankylosaurs

00:03:40.386 --> 00:03:43.765
that proved they used their clubs for fighting each other.

00:03:47.894 --> 00:03:50.897
We are one step closer to fully understanding

00:03:50.897 --> 00:03:53.107
this bizarre-looking dinosaur.

00:03:53.107 --> 00:03:56.444
[MUSIC PLAYING]

